{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fe583ba95e27f88c","name":"Animated Corpse","source":{"id":"source:reference-fe583ba95e27f88c","title":"Animated Corpse","revision":15831,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:16Z","sha256":"1b29a4d079f30e5c2ad8351a7b08b292a33d597bd790e3bb450e1c8ec0f494cd","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15831","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Animated%20Corpse&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fe583ba95e27f88c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Echoes of the Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Echoes_of_the_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:e6a2e80208e1e351"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["You're surrounded by the approaching corpses. Along with their putrefied organic remains, the dark side drips from the reanimated cadavers like saliva from a predatory ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nexu"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nexu","referenceId":"reference:3ed7ed5cc8afcf97"},". Dancing light fills the cavernous eye sockets of their decomposing general as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kel Dor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kel_Dor","referenceId":"reference:fb61f4510d65d959"}," corpse levels its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"}," at you. The undead horde charges."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Called \"Guardian Spirits\" due to primitive cultures' belief that they were the spirits of the dead come back to life, these creatures are actually parasites with telekinetic abilities. Each parasite can inhabit one corpse at a time (as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Guardian Spirit Parasite"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Guardian_Spirit_Parasite","referenceId":"reference:06cbd5f88396461c"},"), giving the body a semblance of undead animation. Simultaneously, each parasite can also reanimate other corpses without actually being in their bodies (as Animated Corpses), but they do so less efficiently, and only to help kill the heroes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The parasites cannot live outside of a host body for long. If the heroes kill a host body, its parasite inhabits one of the remaining Animated Corpses, turning it into a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Guardian Spirit Parasite"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Guardian_Spirit_Parasite","referenceId":"reference:06cbd5f88396461c"},". If there are no Animated Corpses close enough to inhabit, the parasite has nowhere to go and is destroyed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["These cadavers are actually made up of two distinct groups: the salvagers known as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Stalfonauts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Stalfonauts?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and bounty hunters led by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kel Dor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kel_Dor","referenceId":"reference:fb61f4510d65d959"}," Jacen Yar, who had been out to capture Jedi survivors of the orbital bombardment. The two parties ran into each other in the academy library and wound up killing each other in the archive room. Now, controlled by the parasites like string puppets, their skeletal remains remember nothing of their former lives.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Animated Corpse Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"hr